Hi Dominykas,

On your personal user account set your system path to reference /usr/local/bin BEFORE /usr/bin.
e.g. /usr/local/bin:/usr/local/sbin:/bin:/usr/sbin:/sbin:/usr/bin:/usr/X11/bin

Install CRAN R via Homebrew package manager:

brew update ; brew tap homebrew/science ; brew install R

Install RRO 8.0 Beta using the instructions on the MRAN web site <http://mran.revolutionanalytics.com/documents/rro/installation/>.
Now, you can run both:
Run CRAN R by typing /usr/local/bin/R in your terminal.
Run RRO by typing in your terminal /usr/bin/R or just R.

I'd have to experiment with the SublimeText integration to give more info on that hookup.

Hope this helps,
Chris

